\ A runtime definition matching a used module's private helper stays silent on every tier.
\ The baked base scope must not expose module-private words, and the eager guard must not
\ mistake a promoted helper in jit_dispatch for a visible binding.
\
\ A defining word body now gets a transient frame, so this definition runs at top level.
\ The trailing `0 drop` keeps the statement from ending in `;`: freeze collects it for
\ binary runtime, where the definition reaches the durable entry frame on every tier.
\ The real source location is shared by interpreted and AOT diagnostics.

use { via-helper: } "runtime_private_helper_mod.1z" ;

via-helper .

probe-helper: ( -- fixnum ) [ 7 ] ; 0 drop

"defined" print-line
